{
  "description": "Recurring cavity-1 thermal excursions from a partly blocked cooling manifold: three in the week before the investigation, each a body-temperature rise, a reflected-power spike and a forward-power trip from thermal detuning; the last is the beam dump four days ago. Nothing after the manifold repair two days ago, when cavity 1 settles at 26.5 degC. Cavity 2 shows one minor excursion for contrast.",
  "_comment": [
    "Events are placed with `at_when`, the logbook's own {days_ago, time}, so each",
    "excursion lands at the clock time the logbook entries narrate.",
    "Temperature spikes have sigma 2500 s: the trip-day excursion climbs from about",
    "01:00 to 34.2 degC at 03:05 and is back under 30 degC before 04:30. The",
    "forward-power trips are deep dips (sigma 1900 s) centred 47.5 min after each",
    "temperature peak, floored at 0 kW for about 75 min (03:15 to 04:30 on the trip",
    "day). The step at the repair time is the cooling restored; the override keeps",
    "the live reading there."
  ],
